# Review: SidekickPlugin

Only the plugin skeleton is built. It registers two schemas, a skill and one article surface. The
skill `org.dxos.skill.sidekick` carries instructions that describe profiles, the journal, email
and voice tolerance, but it exposes no tools (`toolDefinitions({ operations: [] })`). It does not
compose the database, markdown, agent or inbox skills the spec lists. Nothing creates an Agent, a
chat, a queue, a journal, a memory document or a profile. The dashboard renders all five sections
with hard-coded empty data. Phase 2 (email, comment threads) is not started.

The biggest divergence is in the types. `types/Profile.ts#Profile` and `types/Sidekick.ts#Profile`
both declare the typename `org.dxos.type.sidekick.profile` at 0.1.0 with different fields, and both
are registered in `capabilities/schema.ts`. The surface binds to `Sidekick.Profile` (agent plus
journal refs), not to Agent objects that carry the sidekick skill. The only test checks that the
schema module activates.

Of 50 items: 0 done, 6 untested, 10 partial, 4 diverged, 30 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict Profile: Profile has the spec's fields, but document is Ref<Obj.Unknown> and the typename collides with Sidekick.Profile.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-sidekick/src/types/Profile.ts#Profile, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-sidekick/src/types/Profile.ts#make]
  note: |
    `make` defaults the three flags to false and stamps `lastUpdated`. `types/Sidekick.ts` declares a second class with the
    same typename `org.dxos.type.sidekick.profile` and version, and both are registered. No test creates a Profile.
```

